# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/speed-insights` (v2.0.0)
- **Files modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
- **File modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the body tag of the root layout

## Implementation Details

This project uses **Next.js 16.2.4**, which is compatible with the modern Speed Insights integration approach. Following the documentation's framework-specific instructions for Next.js v13.5+:

1. Used the `@vercel/speed-insights/next` package (Next.js-specific version)
2. Placed the `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root layout's body
3. The component will automatically track page views and performance metrics

### Code Structure
The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout at `src/app/layout.tsx`, which is the appropriate location for Next.js App Router projects. This ensures the tracking is available across all pages of the application.

## Verification Results

✅ **Build Status**: Successfully compiled without errors
- Build completed with Next.js 16.2.4 (Turbopack)
- TypeScript compilation passed
- All 41 routes generated successfully

✅ **Linter**: No new errors introduced
- Pre-existing linting errors in other files (unrelated to this change)
- Speed Insights integration code passes all lint checks

✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file updated correctly
- package-lock.json contains all necessary dependencies
- No conflicts with existing packages

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Navigate to the Speed Insights section in the project settings
3. Click "Enable" to activate the feature
4. The tracking script will be automatically injected at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
5. Performance metrics will start appearing in the dashboard once users visit the site

## Notes

- The integration is zero-config and works automatically once enabled on Vercel
- No additional configuration is required in the code
- The component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- Metrics collection is completely anonymous and GDPR-compliant
